{"nodes": [{"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_gems_qcf_backend_contract", "label": "GEMS QCF Backend Contract Answers", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_gems_server_group", "label": "GEMS Server Group Identification", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "server_groups is a stored per-QCF-row column copied at QCF creation from the RFQ row, never derived at read time, so it is stable and trustworthy. JS comparisons are strict equality with no normalization, so the frontend must match the exact string 'GEMS'.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_cl_approved_at", "label": "cl_approved_at post-CL signal", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "cl_approved_at is the only field that means specifically 'CL approved'; it is destructured in the detail controllers but never placed in headerInformation, so exposing it is a required change.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_qcf_approved", "label": "qcf_approved status flag", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "qcf_approved = 1 is set only after syncAutoPO succeeds, so it means 'PO published', not 'someone approved'; 2 means diverted to Manual Sourcing; null is the normal pending state. It cannot distinguish who approved and must not be used to detect the post-CL state.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_waiting_manual_po", "label": "WAITING_MANUAL_PO milestone 26", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "GEMS currently has no stable post-CL resting state because Auto PO immediately advances milestone 18 to SAP_SYNC_COMPLETE 20; a dedicated milestone 26 gives the Manual PO stage a durable state with po_number left null.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_canapprove", "label": "canApprove capability flag", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "canApprove is computed per endpoint today with two different formulas, so the same field name carries different semantics; moving it to per-authenticated-role is a behavior change the frontend must absorb.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_canmanualsourcing", "label": "canManualSourcing capability flag", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "Return role-aware capability booleans rather than raw fields so the GEMS rule does not have to be reimplemented in two codebases; the backend still enforces the rule server-side, making the booleans a rendering convenience rather than the security boundary.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_management_approval_gap", "label": "Management Approval Eligibility Gap", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "PUT /pr/management/approve_qcf has a role guard but neither controller nor repository checks server group, approval config or prior CL approval; the update predicate is only qcf_number plus three null fields, so Management can approve a GEMS QCF before or after CL and trigger Auto PO.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_manual_sourcing_role_gap", "label": "Manual Sourcing Role Guard Gap", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "POST /pr/cs/send_isourcing has no role guard at all and the handler trusts a client-supplied is_system_action flag; worse, the iSourcing board mutation happens before the RFQ/QCF status updates, so a late rejection would leave an orphaned board card.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_cs_token_access", "label": "CS QCF Detail Token Access", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_unbound_qcf_token", "label": "Unbound QCF Token Risk", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "The QCF token payload carries only qcf_number, rfq_number and vendor_code, so it authorizes a QCF rather than a person; decodeTokenWithForbiddenException verifies only JWT signature and expiry and never consults qcf_token_email, so a revoked token keeps working until the JWT expires.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_sub_category_id_gap", "label": "Missing qcf_library.sub_category_id Join Key", "file_type": "rationale", "rationale": "CS PIC resolution keys on category_matrices.category_id, but qcf_library has no sub_category_id column and insertBulkQcf copies only the sub_category name, so there is no key for any CS authorization or recipient resolution.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_categorymatrixresolver", "label": "categoryMatrixResolver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_buildgemsmanualporecipients", "label": "buildGemsManualPoRecipients", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "A new resolver is added rather than repurposing buildCsRecipients, which puts Sub CS in CC instead of To and is currently unused by any caller.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_approvebycl", "label": "approveByCL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_management_label_map", "label": "MANAGEMENT_LABEL_MAP dashboard mapping", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "At CL_APPROVAL the Management map yields Need Action with action 'Approve / Manual Sourcing', so the default filter surfaces the GEMS row with action buttons rather than hiding it. That is the actual QA defect.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_slacalculator", "label": "slaCalculator token expiry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_error_code", "label": "Machine-readable error_code contract", "file_type": "concept", "rationale": "'Not authorized' and 'not found' are indistinguishable today (both 400 with the not-found message) and expiry vs malformed are both 403, so the frontend routes every failure to /page-expired; a machine-readable error_code lets it branch.", "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_gems_qcf_backend_contract", "target": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_gems_server_group", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "aigen-backend/docs/gems-qcf-manual-po/backend-contract-answers.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "aigen_backend_docs_gems_qcf_manual_po_backend_contract_answers_approvebycl", "target": "aigen